---
import '../styles/global.css';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Contact from '../components/Contact.astro';

const credentials = [
  'ITIL® 4 Foundation',
  'ITIL® 4 Strategist: Direct, Plan & Improve',
  'Microsoft Certified: Azure Fundamentals'
];
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
  <link rel="alternate icon" type="image/x-icon" href="/favicon.ico" />
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#10283b" />
  <meta name="description" content="Explore John White’s experience in IT leadership, infrastructure delivery, service management, continual improvement, and organizational collaboration." />
  <title>Professional Experience | John White</title>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
</head>
<body>
  <Header current="experience" />

  <main>
    <section class="experience-page-intro">
      <div class="container experience-wrap">
        <div class="eyebrow">PROFESSIONAL EXPERIENCE</div>
        <h1>Experience built through practice, responsibility, and continual development.</h1>
        <p class="lead">My career in information technology has grown to encompass technical operations, people leadership, service management, infrastructure delivery, and complex organizational initiatives.</p>
        <p>Across manufacturing, healthcare, and business service environments, I've developed an understanding of how people, technology, processes, and organizational priorities influence one another.</p>
        <nav class="page-jumps" aria-label="Explore experience areas">
          <a href="#leadership">People & Leadership ↗</a>
          <a href="#technology">Technology & Operations ↗</a>
          <a href="#improvement">Continual Improvement ↗</a>
          <a href="#collaboration">Organizational Collaboration ↗</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="experience-band experience-dark" id="leadership">
      <div class="container experience-wrap">
        <div class="eyebrow">01 / PEOPLE & LEADERSHIP</div>
        <h2>Developing People. Strengthening Teams.</h2>
        <p>My approach to leadership has evolved through experience, responsibility, and an understanding that effective leadership requires more than directing work or maintaining a productive team.</p>
        <p>I've recruited, mentored, and developed employees across different stages of their careers, recognizing potential beyond technical qualifications alone. My experience includes building teams, creating opportunities for employees to assume new responsibilities, and supporting their development into more specialized roles.</p>
        <p>I approach leadership with a responsibility to both the individual and the organization, balancing operational requirements with opportunities for professional development.</p>
        <div class="experience-highlights feature-grid">
          <div><h3>Building teams</h3><p>Recruiting, mentoring, and developing capabilities that support effective service delivery.</p></div>
          <div><h3>Recognizing potential</h3><p>Looking beyond credentials and creating opportunities for employees to expand their responsibilities.</p></div>
          <div><h3>Supporting growth</h3><p>Encouraging professional development and helping individuals prepare for future opportunities.</p></div>
        </div>

<details class="experience-accordion">
  <summary>
    <span>Experience in Practice</span>
    <span class="accordion-indicator" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </summary>

  <div class="accordion-content">
    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h3>Building Capabilities, Not Just Teams</h3>
      <p>
        Experience establishing IT functions, rebuilding teams, and
        developing individuals into increasingly specialized roles.
        What began as managing technical responsibilities evolved into
        building teams capable of growing beyond their original
        structure and leadership.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h3>Recognizing Potential Beyond Experience</h3>
      <p>
        Recruiting and mentoring across different organizations revealed
        the importance of identifying adaptability, initiative, and
        interpersonal strengths. These qualities increasingly informed
        how I approached hiring, delegation, and professional development.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h3>Connecting People, Service, and Business Needs</h3>
      <p>
        Leading teams through operational demands, organizational changes,
        and competing priorities broadened my understanding of leadership.
        Technical delivery became one part of a larger responsibility:
        supporting people while strengthening the organization's ability
        to operate and adapt.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>

      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="experience-band experience-light" id="technology">
      <div class="container experience-wrap">
        <div class="eyebrow">02 / TECHNOLOGY & OPERATIONS</div>
        <h2>Building Infrastructure. Enabling Business.</h2>
        <p>Throughout my career, I've led six complete IT infrastructure projects, ranging from facility modernization to establishing technology environments for new manufacturing operations across North America.</p>
        <p>These initiatives have involved infrastructure planning, solution design, budgeting, competitive procurement, vendor coordination, implementation, and migration. Each required balancing technical capabilities with business needs, operational continuity, long-term supportability, and financial considerations.</p>
        <p>My experience also extends into ongoing infrastructure management, cybersecurity, virtualization, service delivery, and business continuity—maintaining and improving the technology environments that support daily operations.</p>
        <div class="experience-highlights feature-grid">
          <div><h3>Infrastructure delivery</h3><p>Remote facility establishment in Alabama and Mexico, infrastructure replacements, and multi-site implementations.</p></div>
          <div><h3>Modernization & resilience</h3><p>Virtualization, staged migrations, redundant systems, and secure infrastructure environments.</p></div>
          <div><h3>Cost & business outcomes</h3><p>Competitive procurement and sustainable solutions, including modernization that avoided over $100,000 in costs.</p></div>
        </div>
        
<details class="experience-accordion">
  <summary>
    <span>Experience in Practice</span>
    <span class="accordion-indicator" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </summary>

  <div class="accordion-content">
    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h3>From Implementation to Infrastructure Strategy</h3>
      <p>
        Experience delivering six complete infrastructure initiatives,
        from modernizing established facilities to building technology
        environments for new manufacturing operations across North America.
        These responsibilities evolved from technical implementation into
        solution architecture, project planning, budgeting, procurement,
        and coordinating delivery across multiple locations.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h3>Modernization with Operational Continuity</h3>
      <p>
        Infrastructure replacements, virtualization, and staged migrations
        strengthened my approach to balancing modernization with business
        continuity. Experience coordinating complex transitions reinforced
        the importance of maintaining operational stability while introducing
        new capabilities, improving resilience, and reducing long-term
        support requirements.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h3>Connecting Technology Investment to Business Value</h3>
      <p>
        Managing infrastructure projects expanded my responsibilities
        beyond technical specifications into competitive procurement,
        lifecycle planning, and financial accountability. These experiences
        included delivering sustainable infrastructure solutions and
        identifying alternatives that avoided more than $100,000 in
        projected costs while meeting operational requirements.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h3>From Infrastructure Delivery to Operational Stewardship</h3>
      <p>
        Supporting technology environments beyond initial implementation
        broadened my focus to cybersecurity, system availability,
        service delivery, recovery capabilities, and operational risk.
        This perspective connects infrastructure decisions with their
        lasting impact on reliability, maintainability, and the
        organization's ability to operate effectively.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>

      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="experience-band experience-dark" id="improvement">
      <div class="container experience-wrap">
        <div class="eyebrow">03 / PROCESSES & CONTINUAL IMPROVEMENT</div>
        <h2>Recognizing Needs. Developing Better Practices.</h2>
        <p>Continual improvement has been a consistent part of how I approach my responsibilities. I look for opportunities to strengthen operations by understanding existing conditions, identifying gaps, and developing practical solutions.</p>
        <p>My experience includes establishing service desk workflows, asset management practices, risk assessment processes, knowledge management systems, and structured approaches to service delivery.</p>
        <p>Many of these practices developed through direct operational experience before I formally studied ITIL. My subsequent ITIL qualifications provided an established framework for practices I had already begun applying.</p>
        <p>I continue to use this combination of practical experience and structured service management principles to support reliability, accountability, and organizational effectiveness.</p>
        <div class="experience-highlights feature-grid">
          <div><h3>Service management</h3><p>Service desk, escalation, incident, and problem management workflows.</p></div>
          <div><h3>Asset & knowledge management</h3><p>Practical systems that improve visibility, documentation, and consistency.</p></div>
          <div><h3>Risk-aware improvement</h3><p>Identifying operational risks and integrating mitigation into ongoing decisions and initiatives.</p></div>
        </div>

        <details class="experience-accordion">
          <summary>
            <span>Experience in Practice</span>
            <span class="accordion-indicator" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </summary>

          <div class="accordion-content">
            <div class="accordion-item">
              <h3>Recognizing Patterns Beyond Individual Problems</h3>
              <p>
                Repeated operational challenges revealed opportunities to
                address underlying processes rather than individual symptoms.
                This perspective shaped my approach to identifying recurring
                issues, improving workflows, and developing solutions that
                strengthen operations beyond the immediate problem.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item">
              <h3>Turning Practical Experience into Structured Practices</h3>
              <p>
                Developed service desk workflows, escalation procedures,
                asset management practices, and knowledge systems through
                direct operational experience. Formal ITIL studies later
                provided a broader framework for understanding, refining,
                and connecting practices already established in the workplace.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item">
              <h3>Making Risk Part of Operational Decisions</h3>
              <p>
                Experience managing infrastructure and service delivery
                expanded my attention from resolving immediate needs to
                recognizing dependencies, single points of failure, and
                longer-term operational risks. This perspective supports
                more informed decisions about priorities, investment,
                resilience, and organizational accountability.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="accordion-item">
              <h3>Improvement Through People and Processes</h3>
              <p>
                Working across different teams and organizations reinforced
                that sustainable improvement depends on more than technical
                solutions. Clear responsibilities, practical documentation,
                shared understanding, and employee involvement help turn
                individual improvements into lasting operational capabilities.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </details>

      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="experience-band experience-light" id="collaboration">
      <div class="container experience-wrap">
        <div class="eyebrow">04 / ORGANIZATIONAL COLLABORATION</div>
        <h2>Working Across Boundaries.</h2>
        <p>My responsibilities have frequently extended beyond individual departments and facilities, requiring collaboration across business functions, management structures, geographic locations, and organizational relationships.</p>
        <p>I've worked with executives, operational leaders, contractors, vendors, and independently managed IT teams to coordinate infrastructure initiatives, support organizational integration, and align technology with business requirements.</p>
        <p>This experience includes supporting international manufacturing operations, coordinating remote facility establishment, and participating in the technical integration of business systems during organizational change.</p>
        <p>These environments have strengthened my ability to understand competing priorities, communicate across different responsibilities, and maintain a broader operational perspective.</p>
      
      <div class="experience-highlights feature-grid">
  <div>
    <h3>Cross-functional collaboration</h3>
    <p>Connecting technical initiatives with operational priorities, business requirements, and organizational objectives.</p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <h3>Multi-site coordination</h3>
    <p>Working across geographic boundaries, management structures, and independently managed teams.</p>
  </div>
  <div>
    <h3>Organizational integration</h3>
    <p>Supporting business transitions, aligning technology environments, and maintaining continuity through change.</p>
  </div>
</div>
      
<details class="experience-accordion">
  <summary>
    <span>Experience in Practice</span>
    <span class="accordion-indicator" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  </summary>

  <div class="accordion-content">
    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h3>Understanding the Business Beyond IT</h3>
      <p>
        Working alongside manufacturing operations, business leaders,
        and service teams expanded my understanding of how technology
        decisions affect the broader organization. This experience
        strengthened my ability to connect technical recommendations
        with operational realities, business priorities, and the
        people responsible for delivering results.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h3>Coordinating Across Organizational Boundaries</h3>
      <p>
        Supporting operations across Canada, the United States, and
        Mexico required collaboration with local leadership, vendors,
        contractors, and independently managed IT teams. These
        experiences developed my ability to coordinate complex
        initiatives while respecting different responsibilities,
        operating environments, and organizational priorities.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h3>Supporting Integration Through Organizational Change</h3>
      <p>
        Participating in business integrations and infrastructure
        transitions broadened my perspective beyond individual
        systems and facilities. Aligning technology, coordinating
        stakeholders, and maintaining operational continuity
        reinforced the importance of communication, shared
        understanding, and adaptability during organizational change.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="accordion-item">
      <h3>Balancing Competing Priorities</h3>
      <p>
        Experience working with executives, operational leaders,
        and technical teams strengthened my ability to navigate
        differing expectations and constraints. My approach
        increasingly emphasizes understanding each perspective,
        communicating business implications, and finding practical
        solutions that serve the organization as a whole.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>

      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="experience-band experience-credentials" id="credentials">
      <div class="container experience-wrap credentials-layout">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">CREDENTIALS & PROFESSIONAL DEVELOPMENT</div>
          <h2>Continuing to Learn. Continuing to Improve.</h2>
          <p>My formal qualifications complement the practical experience I've developed throughout my career.</p>
          <ul class="credential-list">{credentials.map(credential => <li>{credential}</li>)}</ul>
        </div>
        <div class="resume-panel">
          <h3>Professional résumé</h3>
          <p>My résumé provides additional information about employment history, responsibilities, and qualifications.</p>
          <!-- Add your finalized PDF URL to the button below when published. -->
          <a class="button" href="mailto:connect@johnwhite.ca?subject=Resume%20request">Request my résumé →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <Contact variant="experience" />
  </main>
  <Footer />
</body>
</html>

<style>
  .experience-wrap { max-width: 1040px; }
  .experience-page-intro { padding: 96px 0 84px; background: #20445c; color: #fff; }
  .experience-page-intro h1 { font-size: clamp(34px, 4.2vw, 54px); line-height: 1.15; max-width: 880px; margin: 12px 0 26px; }
  .experience-page-intro p { max-width: 790px; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.75; }
  .experience-page-intro .lead { font-weight: 600; }
  
.experience-page-intro .eyebrow {
  color: #a9cfe8;
}

.experience-page-intro h1,
.experience-page-intro p,
.experience-page-intro .page-jumps a {
  color: #ffffff;
}

  .page-jumps { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 10px; margin-top: 32px; }
  .page-jumps a { border: 1px solid #cbd7df; padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; }
  .page-jumps a:hover { border-color: #07599e; color: #07599e; }
  .experience-band { padding: 86px 0 94px; scroll-margin-top: 75px; }
  .experience-band h2 { font-size: clamp(30px, 3.4vw, 43px); line-height: 1.18; margin: 14px 0 25px; }
  .experience-band p { max-width: 820px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.8; margin: 0 0 18px; }
  .experience-dark { background: #163448; color: #f7fbfd; }
  .experience-dark .eyebrow, .experience-credentials .eyebrow { color: #9ed4f5; }
  .experience-light { background: #f0f3f5; color: #13263a; }
  .experience-highlights { margin-top: 42px; padding-top: 28px; border-top: 1px solid currentColor; }
  .experience-highlights h3 { font-size: 17px; letter-spacing: -.025em; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .experience-highlights p { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0; }
  .experience-dark .experience-highlights { border-color: #486577; }
  .experience-light .experience-highlights { border-color: #cbd6dc; }
  .experience-credentials { background: #173c56; color: #fff; }
  .credentials-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.5fr 1fr; gap: 70px; align-items: center; }
  .credential-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 26px 0 0; }
  .credential-list li { border-top: 1px solid #557185; padding: 12px 0; font-weight: 600; }
  .resume-panel { border: 1px solid #648399; border-radius: 8px; padding: 28px; }
  .resume-panel h3 { font-size: 22px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  .resume-panel p { font-size: 14px; }
  .resume-panel .button { margin-top: 8px; }

/* Experience accordion */

.experience-accordion {
  margin-top: 36px;
  border: 1px solid #486577;
  border-radius: 8px;
  overflow: hidden;
}

.experience-accordion summary {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: space-between;
  gap: 16px;
  padding: 20px 24px;
  cursor: pointer;
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: 16px;
  list-style: none;
  transition: background 0.2s ease;
}

.experience-accordion summary::-webkit-details-marker {
  display: none;
}

.experience-accordion summary:hover {
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
}

.accordion-indicator::after {
  content: "+";
  font-size: 24px;
  font-weight: 400;
  line-height: 1;
}

.experience-accordion[open] .accordion-indicator::after {
  content: "−";
}

.accordion-content {
  padding: 8px 24px 24px;
  border-top: 1px solid #486577;
}

.accordion-item {
  padding-top: 20px;
}

.accordion-item + .accordion-item {
  margin-top: 20px;
  border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
}

.accordion-item h3 {
  font-size: 18px;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}

.experience-band .accordion-item p {
  font-size: 15px;
  line-height: 1.75;
  margin-bottom: 0;
}

/* Accordion styling for light experience sections */

.experience-light .experience-accordion {
  border-color: #cbd6dc;
}

.experience-light .experience-accordion summary:hover {
  background: rgba(16, 40, 59, 0.05);
}

.experience-light .accordion-content {
  border-top-color: #cbd6dc;
}

.experience-light .accordion-item + .accordion-item {
  border-top-color: rgba(16, 40, 59, 0.15);
}

  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .experience-page-intro { padding: 64px 0; }
    .experience-band { padding: 62px 0; }
    .experience-highlights { gap: 22px; }
    .credentials-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 22px; }
    .experience-highlights > div + div { padding-top: 18px; border-top: 1px solid #91a4b366; }
  }
</style>
